    "hutton_social_analysis": "Hutton emphasizes that love magic was among the most commonly sought folk magical services, reflecting the high personal stakes of marriage and sexual relationships in a society where marriage determined economic survival and social status. Cunning folk who offered love magic services were responding to genuine demand. The prosecution of love magic was episodic rather than systematic, suggesting i",
    "ginzburg_interrogation_analysis": "Ginzburg's work on Italian inquisitorial records shows that love magic prosecution provides unusually good evidence for genuine folk practice — accused persons described specific clients, specific commissions, specific techniques — in ways that suggest real commercial magical practice rather than interrogation-constructed narratives. Love magic records offer some of the clearest windows into actua",
