    "hutton_social_analysis": "Hutton emphasizes that maleficium accusations were socially embedded accusations arising from specific community relationships of debt, conflict, and dependency. The classic pattern identified by Thomas and Macfarlane — the charity-refused mechanism, the muttered curse, the subsequent misfortune — shows maleficium accusations emerging from the texture of village life rather than from theological d",
